\DOC check_axioms

\TYPE {check_axioms : unit -> unit}

\SYNOPSIS
Checks that no axioms other than the three basic ones have been asserted.

\DESCRIBE
A call {check_axioms()} examines the current list of axioms, as returned by
{axioms()}, and succeeds (returning {()}) if every one of them is one of the
three axioms of the HOL Light core, namely the axiom of infinity
{INFINITY_AX}, the axiom of choice {SELECT_AX} and the extensionality axiom
{ETA_AX}. This gives a simple way of confirming that a development has been
carried out purely by definitional extension, for example at the end of a
proof script.

\FAILURE
Fails if any other axiom has been introduced, e.g. by {new_axiom}. The failure
message lists the extra axioms.

\EXAMPLE
In a fresh HOL Light session, the check succeeds:
{
  # check_axioms();;
  val it : unit = ()
}
\noindent but after asserting an axiom it fails:
{
  # new_axiom `x = 1`;;
  val it : thm = |- x = 1

  # check_axioms();;
  Exception: Failure "check_axioms: [|- x = 1]".
}

\SEEALSO
axioms, new_axiom, mk_thm.

\ENDDOC
